cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "PJM and MISO Cold-Spell Calibration Benchmark: When Cold-Spell Calibration Fails to Transfer"
version: 1.2.0
date-released: 2026-11-22
authors:
  - family-names: Goehner
    given-names: Dresden
    email: dresdengoehner@outlook.com
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher, Jurupa Valley, CA, USA"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/DresdenGman/PJM-Cold-Calibration-Benchmark"
abstract: >-
  Code, frozen protocol, derived data and full results for a benchmark of
  probabilistic load forecasting in extreme cold: 13 modelled events in PJM
  and MISO from 2014 to 2026, plus a 2015 operator-error anchor. Three
  forecasters and eight recalibration methods are evaluated under strictly
  chronological evaluation and under retrospective leave-one-event-out
  transfer. Version 1.2.0 adds amendments A5-A8 (ensemble-spread calibrator,
  seven further events, temperature-weighted conformal and extreme-value
  tails, and the benchmark refitted on day-ahead GEFS forecasts), whose plans
  were published here before their data or analyses, and all figure scripts.
keywords:
  - probabilistic load forecasting
  - conformal prediction
  - calibration transfer
  - extreme cold events
  - PJM
  - MISO
  - forecast evaluation
